cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SOMA-S1, please cite it as below."
title: "SOMA-S1: A From-Scratch Somali Foundation Language Model with Sparse Mixture-of-Experts and Multi-head Latent Attention"
authors:
  - given-names: Abdullahi
    family-names: Abshir Boore
    website: https://boore.dev
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: Apache-2.0
type: model
keywords:
  - somali
  - low-resource
  - mixture-of-experts
  - multi-head-latent-attention
  - from-scratch
  - foundation-model
abstract: >-
  SOMA-S1 is a 126.19M-parameter (69.57M active) decoder-only foundation model
  pretrained from scratch on the Somali NLP Corpus, pairing a sparse
  Mixture-of-Experts feed-forward stack with Multi-head Latent Attention and a
  custom 60,000-token byte-level BPE tokenizer. The run processed 1.0758B token
  positions over 16,413 optimizer steps in BF16 on two RTX 3090 GPUs; validation
  cross-entropy reached 3.76 before the run ended by host-side disk exhaustion.
